\details{
S7 class for two-level mediation with \eqn{k \ge 2}{k >= 2} parallel mediators, all measured on level-1 units
nested in clusters (1-1-1), with the paths estimated separately at the within and the between level (latent
cluster means, fixed slopes). It is the parallel counterpart of \link{TwoLevelMediationData}: a separate class, so
the one-mediator object keeps its scalar paths. Every property other than the paths and \code{mediators} has the
meaning it has there.

Per level \eqn{l} the specific indirect effect through \eqn{M_j} is
\eqn{a_{jl} b_{jl}}{a_jl * b_jl}, the total indirect effect is
\eqn{\sum_j a_{jl} b_{jl}}{sum_j a_jl * b_jl} and the direct effect is \eqn{c'_l}{c'_l}. When the between
level cannot be identified the object is \strong{within-only}: the between path vectors hold \code{NA_real_} (still
named by \code{mediators}), \code{c_prime_between} is \code{NA_real_}, and the between rows are absent from \code{estimates} and
\code{vcov}.

The alias rows of \code{estimates} and \code{vcov} are, per level, \verb{a_<M>_within} for each mediator, then
\verb{b_<M>_within}, then \code{c_prime_within}, and the same set with \verb{_between}.
